tate of  this means that your carbohydrate and  protein consumption is low enough  effectively zero in the case of  carbohydrates and your fat intake is  high enough so we're talking about 75  plus percent of your calories from fat  that your body switches into effectively  a starvation mode where it says we're  not getting the carbohydrates and  nutrients we need to produce a glucose  for the body for the brain and  everything else so we're going to start  converting fat that includes stored fat  that's why you store fat into these  alternate fuel source called ketones  okay this is a very very binary thing so  you are either in ketosis or you are not  and we can measure it with say a finger  prick device called the precision extra  X pra by Abbott Labs and if you are not  say at 0.5 millimolar so that's how the  concentration is measured that's the  number Rita if you're not at 0.5 or  higher and if you're in ketosis  generally people who consider the  fueling the euphoria and the clarity  that you feel at say 1 millimolar or  higher for some people it's even 1.5 or  2 you are in ketosis but a lot of people  and when I say a lot I would say more  than 60% of people who attempt to do  this will fail because they will miss  things like some type of sugar that's in  the mustard they use or they will have  some type of even say non-nutritive  artificial sweetener that for whatever  reason provokes an insulin response or  glucose response or this is a trickier  one they aren't consuming a bunch of  carbohydrates they followed that but  they're eating too much protein and then  the liver turns the extra amino acids  via something called gluconeogenesis  into [ __ ] boot pardon my french glucose  and then you're screwed again so there  are many ways to mess up the ketogenic  diet and if you think you're in ketosis  so you're eating 7080 percent of your  calories from fat but you're actually  using glucose that is arguably the worst  possible by it you could follow your  